From a08f3a26b9fe218828a4871ea0a30480c57a0631 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 20:11:38 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [GUI] GUIFontTTFGLES: do not pop a modelview matrix that was
 never pushed

CGUIFontTTFGLES::LastEnd() calls glMatrixModview.Pop() once for each block of
text it draws, but it never pushes that stack: it computes the matrix of each
block locally (projection * modelview * GUI matrix * translation) and sends it
to the shader. The Pop() is left over from an older version that pushed a
translated modelview around each block; the OpenGL version of the same function
(GUIFontTTFGL.cpp) has neither.

CMatrixGLStack::Pop() does nothing on an empty stack, which is the case for all
text the GUI draws, so nothing goes wrong today. But when text is drawn while a
caller holds a pushed level (an add-on screensaver window keeps one from its
GUI_MSG_WINDOW_INIT to its GUI_MSG_WINDOW_DEINIT, around CaptureStateBlock() and
ApplyStateBlock(); a renderer that draws text over a pushed transform), the
first block of text takes that level: the caller's matrix is restored in the
middle of its drawing, every later block of text is placed with it, and the
caller's own PopLoad() then restores nothing. The CroqueMr fork met it as
subtitles that disappeared in the black bars, with a modelview pushed around
its own drawing of them.

Remove the Pop(). Nothing in the function changes the modelview stack, so
nothing has to be restored.
---
 xbmc/guilib/GUIFontTTFGLES.cpp | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/xbmc/guilib/GUIFontTTFGLES.cpp b/xbmc/guilib/GUIFontTTFGLES.cpp
index fa9aca0..720788f 100644
--- a/xbmc/guilib/GUIFontTTFGLES.cpp
+++ b/xbmc/guilib/GUIFontTTFGLES.cpp
@@ -272,8 +272,6 @@ void CGUIFontTTFGLES::LastEnd()
         glDrawElements(GL_TRIANGLES, 6 * count, GL_UNSIGNED_SHORT, 0);
         CRenderSystemBase::m_GUIElementCount++;
       }
-
-      glMatrixModview.Pop();
     }
     // Restore the original scissor rectangle
     if (m_scissorClip)
-- 
2.53.0

